{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And Moses said: This thing, etc.</b> One needs to know what it means by saying <b>the thing</b>. Further, one needs to know to whom Moses is commanding this commandment — if to Aaron, behold it says afterward ״וַיֹּאמֶר מֹשֶׁה״ etc. And further, a doubling of words appears to me here." "It appears that Moses' intention is along this line: <b>This is the thing that YHWH commanded, etc. — a full omer, etc.</b> — but HaShem did not say who would take it, nor did He state the procedure for taking it, nor did He state the place of its deposit. Rather, this alone is the statement that went forth from the mouth of YHWH to me, and nothing more. ״And he said to Aaron״ — he judged with the justice of a wise man's understanding, for the meaning of ״לְמִשְׁמֶרֶת״ (״for safekeeping״) bears two interpretations, and it is the way of the Torah that whenever a word can bear two equally-weighted meanings, it intends both, whichever of them you derive. And the two interpretations are: the first — safekeeping from impurity; and the second — safekeeping from pilferage (shelichut yad). Corresponding to pilferage, he specified the place of safekeeping in the Tent of Meeting — there, a place where the needs of Israel are located: the Torah and the vessels of service — and this too is an instrument that serves to provide instruction of a matter that HaShem wishes to show to generations. And similarly did HaShem with Aaron's staff and with the firepans of Korah's assembly (Numbers 17:25, 17:3–4); therefore he said to place it ״before YHWH.״ And corresponding to guarding against impurity, he said ״one jar,״ and they of blessed memory said (Mekhilta): a jar (tzintzenet) is something that produces a sound (matzitz) from its fellow — it is an earthen vessel, and whenever a tightly fitted lid is fastened upon it, it is pure. And these two details he heard from the word of YHWH in His saying ״לְמִשְׁמֶרֶת,״ and from this he reasoned that Aaron is the one to take it, for he is the priest who serves in the Sanctuary — therefore ״וַיֹּאמֶר אֶל אַהֲרֹן.״ And lest the people think that HaShem had said to him to speak to Aaron ״וְלָקַחְתָּ צִנְצֶנֶת״ etc., therefore the great faithful one said ״This is the thing that YHWH commanded״ — and nothing more — and the wise man understood the intention." "<b>Or</b> it may mean that at first, when he received the prophecy, he presented it before Israel in the order of its hearing from the Most High El — and there was lacking the specification of who would do it, and the place of deposit of the manna, and the place of deposit of the vessel, and he did not know what to do until the prophecy came a second time and he stated his uncertainties to Him. And this is what it says at the end of the account: <b>as YHWH commanded Moses</b> (Exodus 16:34) — meaning, do not suppose in your mind that the details that are not explicitly stated in the word of YHWH — being the three that are mentioned — Moses did on his own initiative. Not so; rather, as YHWH commanded Moses, from the mouth of the Most High, so were the things." "And according to the first interpretation, His saying <b>as YHWH commanded, etc.</b> is to be explained as the verse intending to say that Moses' reasoning was vindicated — as though HaShem had so commanded him, according to how he judged the concealed matters as we have explained." "<b>For safekeeping for your generations.</b> It speaks in plural language: one was in the generation of Jeremiah, and one will exist in the time to come, as they of blessed memory said (Mekhilta 21, Tanhuma 3): three things is Elijah destined to establish for Israel, and one of them is the flask of manna."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:29:13.973066967Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}